      "id": 35545,
      "name": "flamethrower49",
      "username": "flamethrower49",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-07-29T19:38:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My fiancee went nuts with this idea.  Here are the ideas we had that had some merit.</p>\n<p>Haka’s Vitality Surge - Kiwi Jello Shots<br>\nBunker’s Baked Battery - Baked Potatoes, wrapped in foil, with a spread of options for “Upgrading”<br>\nTempest - Sushi!     (I noted that he may not appreciate that, because it might talk to him.  She didn’t care.)<br>\nRa’s Fireballs - Strawberries covered in sour cream and brown sugar.  (I didn’t know it was a thing, but it’s apparently very good.)<br>\nFanatic’s Angel Food Cake<br>\nAbsolute Zero’s Thermal Shockwave: Baked Alaska or Bananas Flambe, or any flaming dessert.</p>\n<p>These other ideas aren’t as fleshed out.</p>\n<p>Tachyon - Fast food.  (Ha, ha.)  Some sort of appetizer.  Sliders or pizza rolls might be good.<br>\nLegacy - Something All-American is as far as she got.  Apple pie is a strong contender.<br>\nWraith - Something rich.  Maybe involves chocolate.<br>\nExpatriette - She seems like a steak girl.<br>\nMister Fixer - Dumplings.<br>\nNightmist - Fried Calamari?<br>\nUnity - Gingerbread cookies.</p>\n<p>No ideas yet Argent Adept or Visionary.</p>\n<p>We won’t be having these at the wedding.  But we are beginning to give very strong consideration to a themed party sometime after.</p>",
